{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790963583,"nonce":"uqOQ8Voqfc9quHWWGu9D+F9vVVg=","title":"Overrides and interface implementations with a variant signature get no slot adapter","message":"Rows: Issue9836, TestInterface (`eq(py.getY(), 5)` prints 1.3), Issue8528 (`foo`/`bar`).\n\n`ensure_vtable_dispatch_thunk` (ir/mir/decl/vtables.rs) forwards the IMPLEMENTING method's own\nsignature, while the caller (`try_virtual_dispatch`, ir/mir/expr/call/virtual_dispatch.rs, or an\ninterface slot call) uses the base/interface signature and the static expression type.\n\n- `Child.variant():Int` overriding `Parent.variant():Float`: the caller reads a stale float register.\n- `override f(i:Float)` of `f(i:Int)`: the caller passes an i32, the body reads an f64.\n- `A.foo():A` implementing `I.foo():I`: the slot returns a raw object, the caller treats it as a\n  fat pointer. `A.bar(a:I)` implementing `I.bar(a:A)` receives a raw object where it expects a fat pointer.\n\nFix shape: the slot ABI is the signature of the method that introduced the slot (the interface\nmethod for interface slots). The thunk adapts params and return (Int\u003c-\u003eFloat, object\u003c-\u003efat pointer)\nwhen the implementation differs, and the virtual call site calls with that ABI and converts the\nresult to the static type. Fails the same way on LLVM.\n\n```haxe\nprivate class Parent { public function new() {} public function variant(i:Int):Float return 0.0; }\nprivate class Child extends Parent { override function variant(f:Float):Int return 1; }\nprivate class P2 { public function new() {} public function f(i:Int):Float return 0.0; }\nprivate class C2 extends P2 { override function f(i:Float):Float return i + 1.0; }\nclass Main { static function main() {\n  var p:Parent = new Child();\n  Sys.println(p.variant(0));      // 1\n  var p2:P2 = new C2();\n  Sys.println(p2.f(41));          // 42\n}}\n```","files":null}]}